hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"349","Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala and Saeed bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Makhzoumi told us, they said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Labid, on the authority of Abu Salama Ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Ibn Umar, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Do not let the Bedouins prevail over you in the name of your prayers. They are covering the camels, it is the evening prayer.”"
